{
  "id": "pratihara",
  "title": "The Gurjara-Pratiharas",
  "description": "Three centuries of north India: the Pratiharas hold back Arab armies from Sindh, win Kannauj in the three-way struggle with the Palas and Rashtrakutas, rule the north under Mihira Bhoja, then lose their vassals and their capital to Mahmud of Ghazni.",
